.TH LITTLE-WD 1 "November 6, 2026" "little-watchdog"
.SH NAME
little\-wd \- small homelab watchdog with Telegram alarms
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B little\-wd
.RB [ \-config
.IR path ]
.br
.B little\-wd
.RB { run | status | check }
.RB [ \-config
.IR path ]
.br
.B little\-wd
.RB { version | \-\-version | \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B little\-wd
watches hosts (ping), web pages, TCP ports and the machine it runs on.
It sends a Telegram message when a check fails and when it is back.
The watching is done by a systemd service, which runs
.BR "little\-wd run" ;
the other commands set it up and show what it sees.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
(none)
Open the full-screen program: status of all checks, and setup.
It needs a terminal.
Press
.B ?
for the keys.
Quitting does not stop the service.
.TP
.B run
Run the watchdog in the foreground.
The service does this; run it by hand only to try something.
It waits for a usable config instead of failing.
SIGHUP re-reads the config, SIGINT and SIGTERM stop it.
.TP
.B status
Print the last results from the state file as a table.
Runs no check.
Adds a STALE line when the service has not reported lately.
.TP
.B check
Run every check once and print one line per check.
Sends nothing to Telegram and writes no state.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.PP
.B little\-wd help
is the same as
.BR \-\-help .
.B little\-wd
.I command
.B \-h
shows the help of one command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Config file.
Default: the value of
.BR LITTLE_WATCHDOG_CONFIG ,
else
.IR /etc/little\-watchdog/little\-watchdog.env .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/little\-watchdog/little\-watchdog.env
The config, one
.IB KEY = value
per line.
Group
.B little\-wd
may edit it.
.TP
.I /etc/little\-watchdog/little\-watchdog.env.bak
The config as it was before
.B little\-wd
saved its first change in a run.
.TP
.I /var/lib/little\-watchdog/state.json
The state: results, since when, the 24 hour history.
Written about every 10 minutes.
With
.B STATE_IN_RAM=yes
it lives in the runtime directory instead.
.TP
.I /run/little\-watchdog/
The runtime directory, in RAM, made by the service.
It holds the heartbeat
.RI ( state.json.alive )
and the last 30 minutes of every measurement
.RI ( state.json.fine ).
Without
.B RUNTIME_DIRECTORY
(\fBlittle\-wd run\fR started by hand) both files lie next to the state file.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/little\-watchdog.service
The unit (\fI/etc/systemd/system/\fR if installed from the tar.gz).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/little\-watchdog/examples/little\-watchdog.env.example
An example config.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LITTLE_WATCHDOG_CONFIG
Config file, when
.B \-config
is not given.
.TP
.B RUNTIME_DIRECTORY
Absolute path of the runtime directory; systemd sets it for the service.
If unset, the commands look in
.IR /run/little\-watchdog ,
and \fBrun\fR writes nothing there.
.TP
.B LITTLE_WATCHDOG_DEBUG
If set, \fBrun\fR logs a few extra lines.
.TP
.BR GOMAXPROCS ", " GOMEMLIMIT
For
.BR run :
if unset, it uses one thread and a soft memory limit of 24 MiB.
.TP
.BR NO_COLOR ", " TERM ", " COLORTERM ", " LC_ALL ", " LC_CTYPE ", " LANG
Colours and characters of the full-screen program.
.B NO_COLOR
turns colours off; without a UTF-8 locale it draws plain ASCII.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.B run
exits with 0 after SIGINT or SIGTERM.
.B status
exits with 0 whenever it could read the state,
also when checks fail or the service is STALE.
.B check
exits with 0 only if all checks are OK.
.TP
.B 1
An error: the config or state cannot be read, a check failed
.RB ( check ),
or the program cannot run.
.TP
.B 2
A wrong command or option, or no terminal for the full-screen program.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up and look at the checks:
.PP
.RS
.nf
little\-wd
.fi
.RE
.PP
Print the state from a script, and test whether all is well:
.PP
.RS
.nf
little\-wd status
little\-wd check && echo all OK
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use another config file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
little\-wd check \-config ./test.env
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
.PP
Documentation:
.I /usr/share/doc/little\-watchdog/README.md
and, in the source, docs/setup.md (first steps),
docs/config.md (all config keys)
and docs/screens.md (the full-screen program).
.PP
